IMPORT prelude

-- Wills Act 1970 (Western Australia) -- what a will may do (s 6), the age of capacity (s 7), execution and witnesses (ss 8, 10, 11),
-- the deleted s 13, revocation by marriage, by the ending of a marriage and by act of the testator (ss 14, 14A, 15), the other routes to
-- formal validity (s 17, s 20, Part XA, Part X ss 32-33, Part XI s 40), and what happens to a gift whose beneficiary dies first
-- (ss 26(1)(b), (g), 27).
--
-- Edition: compilation from legislation.wa.gov.au (mrdoc 49116, retrieved 7 September 2026), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_49116.txt. The deposit names no compilation number; its compilation table ends with the Legal
-- Profession Uniform Law Application Act 2022 s 424 (in force 1 July 2022), the last reprint listed is Reprint 5 as at 10 July 2015,
-- and the uncommenced provisions table lists the Assisted Reproductive Technology and Surrogacy Act 2025 Pt 17 Div 15 (not shown).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement au/wa:REQ-0003 (priority 1), raised 9 times by the three Western Australian cradle-to-grave lives
-- (Chloe c025, c082, c087, c096, c098; Jake k084; Daniel d074, d085, d086). The lives ask: what may Chloe do at 18 (s 7); the
-- formalities of a will and gifts to witnesses (ss 8, 13); is a parent's will valid (s 8); does a child take anything when the will
-- gives everything to the surviving spouse; what may a will do with a trust; does an Australian will reach a house in Calabria. SCOPED
-- to those provisions, with the definitions, conditions and exceptions needed to answer them.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: s 9 (powers of appointment exercised by will); s 16 (revival); ss 21, 24, 25, 26(1)(a), (c)-(f), 28, 28A
-- (construction); Part IX (relationships); the Annex to the Convention beyond the one flag; ss 41-48 (procedure for and recognition of
-- statutory wills); s 50 (rectification). Probate and intestacy are the Administration Act 1903; claims against an estate are the
-- Family Provision Act 1972; whether the home held jointly or a superannuation balance passes by the will is a question for the law
-- governing that property, not this Act. Whether Italian law governs succession to an Italian house is not answered by this Act:
-- s 20 speaks only to whether a will is "properly executed".
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Wills Act 1970 (WA) -- making, revoking and reading a will`

§§ `helpers`

-- Dates are written as whole numbers YYYYMMDD (2021-03-14 is 20210314), so later dates are larger numbers.
GIVEN `birth year` IS A NUMBER, `birth month` IS A NUMBER, `birth day` IS A NUMBER, `on year` IS A NUMBER, `on month` IS A NUMBER, `on day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`age in completed years` MEANS
    IF `on month` GREATER THAN `birth month` OR (`on month` EQUALS `birth month` AND `on day` AT LEAST `birth day`)
    THEN `on year` MINUS `birth year`
    ELSE `on year` MINUS `birth year` MINUS 1

-- Commencement dates read from the deposit's compilation table and Other notes.
-- The Acts Amendment (Equality of Status) Act 2003, which deleted s 13, came into operation on 1 July 2003; note 1 sets out its
-- s 211(2): the repeal applies to the will of any person dying on or after that commencement.
-- The Wills Amendment Act 2007 is shown as commencing 9 February 2008; the table's entry reads "s. 324", taken here (INFERENCE)
-- to be ss 3-24, which includes s 13 (inserting s 14A) and s 23 (inserting ss 32, 33).
`section 13 repeal commencement` MEANS 20030701
`Wills Amendment Act 2007 commencement` MEANS 20080209

§§ `6 -- what a will may do`

-- s 6: "A person may, by a will executed or made in a manner required or permitted by this Act -- (a) dispose of property (whether
-- acquired before or after the making of the will) to which at the time of the person's death the person is entitled either at law
-- or in equity; and (b) dispose of property that in exercise of a power of appointment the person is entitled or able to dispose of
-- by will; and (c) appoint a guardian of any infant child of the person."
-- s 4: "disposition includes a gift, devise, bequest or an appointment of property contained in a will".
--
-- The Act says nothing about trusts as such. A gift to trustees on trust is still a disposition of property, so (INFERENCE) a will
-- may set up a testamentary trust of property within s 6(a); its terms are a matter for the general law, not this Act.
DECLARE Provision IS ONE OF
    `a gift of property the testator owns at death`
    `a gift of property acquired after the will was made`
    `a gift on trust of property the testator owns at death`
    `an appointment under a power exercisable by will`
    `a guardian for an infant child`
    `a gift of property the testator is not entitled to at death`

GIVEN `the provision` IS A Provision
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 6 lets a will make the provision` IF
    CONSIDER `the provision`
    WHEN `a gift of property the testator is not entitled to at death` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `7 -- age of capacity`

-- s 7: "Subject to section 17, a will made by a person under the age of 18 years is not valid."
-- There is no exception for a married minor, and no court leave. s 7 is not made subject to Part X, so (on the text) a document the
-- Supreme Court accepts under s 32 is still not valid if its maker was under 18. Compare s 40(2)(b): the Court may not authorise a
-- statutory will for a person who has not reached 18.
GIVEN `age when the will was made` IS A NUMBER, `a privileged will saved by section 17` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 7 is satisfied` IF
        `age when the will was made` AT LEAST 18
    OR  `a privileged will saved by section 17`

§§ `8, 11 -- execution and witnesses`

-- s 8: "Subject to sections 17 and 20 and Parts XA, X and XI, a will is not valid unless -- (a) it is in writing; and (b) it is signed
-- by the testator or signed in the testator's name by some other person in the testator's presence and by the testator's direction,
-- in such place on the will so that it is apparent on the face of the will that the testator intended to give effect by the
-- signature to the writing signed as the testator's will; and (c) the testator makes or acknowledges the signature in the presence
-- of at least 2 witnesses present at the same time; and (d) the witnesses attest and subscribe the will in the presence of the
-- testator but no publication or form of attestation is necessary."
-- s 11: "A person who is unable to see and attest that a testator has signed a document cannot act as a witness to a will."
--
-- Nothing in s 8 or s 11 disqualifies a beneficiary, or a beneficiary's spouse, as a witness. The field below is recorded so that the
-- cases can show it changes nothing.
DECLARE Execution HAS
    `in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `signed by the testator` IS A BOOLEAN
    `signed for the testator in their presence and by their direction` IS A BOOLEAN
    `placed so the intent to execute is apparent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `witnesses present at the same time` IS A NUMBER
    `of them, unable to see the testator sign` IS A NUMBER
    `witnesses attested and subscribed in the testator's presence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a witness takes a gift under the will` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the execution` IS AN Execution
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 8 is complied with` IF
        `the execution`'s `in writing`
    AND (    `the execution`'s `signed by the testator`
         OR  `the execution`'s `signed for the testator in their presence and by their direction`)
    AND `the execution`'s `placed so the intent to execute is apparent`
    AND `the execution`'s `witnesses present at the same time` MINUS `the execution`'s `of them, unable to see the testator sign` AT LEAST 2
    AND `the execution`'s `witnesses attested and subscribed in the testator's presence`

§§ `17, 20, Parts XA, X and XI -- the other routes to a valid will`

-- s 20(1): "A will is taken to be properly executed if its execution conforms to the internal law in force in the place -- (a) where it
-- was executed; or (b) that was the testator's domicile or habitual residence, either at the time the will was executed, or at the
-- testator's death; or (c) of which the testator was a national, either at the date of execution of the will, or at the testator's
-- death." (2)(b): "a will, so far as it disposes of immovable property, if it has been executed in conformity with the internal law in
-- force in the place where the property is situated".
-- Part XA: s 32B gives the Annex "the force of law"; Annex Art 1: a will "shall be valid as regards form ... if it is made in the form
-- of an international will complying with the provisions set out in Articles 2 to 5".
-- Part X, s 32(2): a document "even though it has not been executed in the manner required by this Act" constitutes a will "if the
-- Supreme Court is satisfied that the person intended the document to constitute the person's will". s 33(1): s 32 "applies only to
-- persons dying on or after" the commencement of s 23 of the Wills Amendment Act 2007.
-- Part XI, s 40(4): a court-authorised will "must be signed by the Principal Registrar and sealed with the seal of the Court"; s 39(2)
-- takes it to be executed in a manner permitted by this Act.
-- s 17: a will made under the repealed s 18 before its repeal "has effect as if the repeal had not occurred".
DECLARE OtherRoute HAS
    `conforms to the law of the place of execution, domicile, habitual residence or nationality` IS A BOOLEAN
    `conforms to the law where the immovable is` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an international will complying with Annex Articles 2 to 5` IS A BOOLEAN
    `signed by the Principal Registrar and sealed under section 40(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Supreme Court is satisfied the deceased intended it as their will` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a privileged will saved by section 17` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the route` IS AN OtherRoute, `as to an immovable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 20 treats the will as properly executed` IF
        `the route`'s `conforms to the law of the place of execution, domicile, habitual residence or nationality`
    OR  (`as to an immovable` AND `the route`'s `conforms to the law where the immovable is`)

-- `date of death` is 0 while the testator is living.
GIVEN `the execution` IS AN Execution, `the route` IS AN OtherRoute, `as to an immovable` IS A BOOLEAN, `date of death` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the will is formally valid` IF
        `section 8 is complied with` `the execution`
    OR  `section 20 treats the will as properly executed` `the route` `as to an immovable`
    OR  `the route`'s `an international will complying with Annex Articles 2 to 5`
    OR  `the route`'s `signed by the Principal Registrar and sealed under section 40(4)`
    OR  `the route`'s `a privileged will saved by section 17`
    OR  (    `the route`'s `the Supreme Court is satisfied the deceased intended it as their will`
         AND `date of death` AT LEAST `Wills Amendment Act 2007 commencement`)

GIVEN `age when the will was made` IS A NUMBER, `the execution` IS AN Execution, `the route` IS AN OtherRoute, `as to an immovable` IS A BOOLEAN, `date of death` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the will is valid under sections 7 and 8` IF
        `section 7 is satisfied` `age when the will was made` (`the route`'s `a privileged will saved by section 17`)
    AND `the will is formally valid` `the execution` `the route` `as to an immovable` `date of death`

§§ `10 -- alterations after execution`

-- s 10(2): "Subject to Part X, an alteration to a will after it has been executed is not effective unless the alteration is executed in
-- a manner in which a will is required or permitted to be executed by this Act." (3): "Subsection (2) does not apply to an alteration
-- to a will made by, or at the direction of, the testator if the words or effect of the will are no longer apparent because of the
-- alteration." (1): apparent means "legible by the unaided eye or with the help of a magnifying lens but not otherwise".
GIVEN `executed as a will` IS A BOOLEAN, `by or at the direction of the testator, leaving the words no longer apparent` IS A BOOLEAN, `accepted by the Supreme Court under Part X` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 10 does not defeat the alteration` IF
        `executed as a will`
    OR  `by or at the direction of the testator, leaving the words no longer apparent`
    OR  `accepted by the Supreme Court under Part X`

§§ `13 (deleted) -- gifts to witnesses`

-- The deposit shows only: "s. 13 deleted: No. 28 of 2003 s. 211(1)". Its text is not in the deposit, so what it said is not encoded;
-- the lives call it "gifts to witnesses". Note 1 quotes s 211(2): "The repeal effected by subsection (1) applies to and in respect of
-- the will of any person dying on or after the date of the commencement of this section ... but does not apply to the will of a
-- person who died before that date." The compilation table gives that commencement as 1 July 2003.
GIVEN `date of death` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the deleted section 13 can still apply to the will` IF
    `date of death` LESS THAN `section 13 repeal commencement`

§§ `14, 14A -- revocation by marriage and by its ending`

-- s 14(1): "A will is revoked by the marriage of the testator except where -- (a) it is made in contemplation of the marriage; or (b) the
-- will is made in exercise of a power of appointment where the property thereby appointed would not in default of appointment pass to
-- the testator's personal representatives as such." (3): in contemplation if "(a) it is expressed to be made in contemplation of the
-- marriage; or (b) there is other evidence establishing" it. (2): a will in contemplation "is void if the marriage is not solemnised,
-- unless the will provides to the contrary".
GIVEN `the testator married after making the will` IS A BOOLEAN, `made in contemplation of that marriage` IS A BOOLEAN, `an appointment that would not pass to the personal representatives` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 14 revokes the will` IF
        `the testator married after making the will`
    AND (NOT `made in contemplation of that marriage`)
    AND (NOT `an appointment that would not pass to the personal representatives`)

GIVEN `made in contemplation of a marriage` IS A BOOLEAN, `the marriage was solemnised` IS A BOOLEAN, `the will provides to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 14(2) makes the will void` IF
        `made in contemplation of a marriage`
    AND (NOT `the marriage was solemnised`)
    AND (NOT `the will provides to the contrary`)

-- s 14A(2): "A will is revoked by the ending of the testator's marriage except where -- (a) a contrary intention appears in the will;
-- or (b) there is other evidence establishing such an intention." (3): a marriage ends "(a) when a divorce order terminating the
-- marriage takes effect under the Family Law Act; or (b) on the granting of a decree of nullity ...; or (c) on the dissolution or
-- annulment of the marriage in accordance with the law of a place outside Australia, but only if that dissolution or annulment is
-- recognised in Australia". (4): applies where the marriage ends on or after the commencement of s 13 of the Wills Amendment Act 2007.
-- Separation is not an ending; nor, on this list, is the death of the spouse.
DECLARE Ending IS ONE OF
    `a divorce order taking effect`
    `a decree of nullity`
    `a recognised foreign dissolution or annulment`
    `an unrecognised foreign dissolution`
    `separation without a divorce order`
    `the death of the spouse`

GIVEN `the event` IS AN Ending
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the marriage ends for section 14A` IF
    CONSIDER `the event`
    WHEN `a divorce order taking effect` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a decree of nullity` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a recognised foreign dissolution or annulment` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the event` IS AN Ending, `date it happened` IS A NUMBER, `contrary intention in the will` IS A BOOLEAN, `other evidence of that intention` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 14A revokes the will` IF
        `the marriage ends for section 14A` `the event`
    AND `date it happened` AT LEAST `Wills Amendment Act 2007 commencement`
    AND (NOT `contrary intention in the will`)
    AND (NOT `other evidence of that intention`)

§§ `15 -- how else a will is revoked`

-- s 15: "the whole or any part of a will may be revoked only -- (a) by a later will, including a document that is a will by operation of
-- Part X; or (b) subject to Part X, by some writing declaring an intention to revoke it, executed in the manner in which a will is
-- required or permitted to be executed by this Act; or (c) by the testator, or some person in the testator's presence and by the
-- testator's direction, burning, tearing or otherwise destroying it to give effect to the intention of the testator of revoking it."
DECLARE Revocation IS ONE OF
    `a later will`
    `a later document accepted under Part X`
    `a writing declaring revocation, executed as a will`
    `destruction by the testator intending to revoke`
    `destruction by another in the testator's presence and by direction, intending to revoke`
    `destruction by another out of the testator's presence`
    `accidental destruction`
    `an unwitnessed note saying the will is revoked`
    `telling the family the will is revoked`

GIVEN `the act` IS A Revocation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 15 lets the act revoke the will` IF
    CONSIDER `the act`
    WHEN `destruction by another out of the testator's presence` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `accidental destruction` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an unwitnessed note saying the will is revoked` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `telling the family the will is revoked` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `26(1)(b), (g), 27 -- a beneficiary who dies first`

-- s 27(1): "Unless the contrary intention appears by the will, where -- (a) there is a disposition in a will to a person who is a child or
-- other issue of the testator, for an estate or interest not determinable at or before the death of that person; and (b) that person
-- dies in the lifetime of the testator leaving a child or children who survive the testator, the disposition does not lapse but takes
-- effect as a substitutional disposition to such of the children of that person as survive the testator and if more than one in equal
-- shares." (3): "This section does not apply to a disposition to a person as one of 2 or more joint tenants."
-- s 26(1)(g): "if any part of a disposition in fractional parts of the whole or of the residue of the estate of a testator fails, the part
-- that fails accrues to the part that does not fail".
-- s 26(1)(b): property in a disposition "that is void or fails to take effect is to be included in any residuary disposition".
-- What becomes of property the will does not dispose of is not in this Act (the Administration Act 1903 governs intestacy).
DECLARE Gift HAS
    `the beneficiary survived the testator` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the beneficiary is a child or other issue of the testator` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the interest was not determinable at or before the beneficiary's death` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the beneficiary left a child who survived the testator` IS A BOOLEAN
    `given to the beneficiary as a joint tenant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a fractional share of the whole or residue, and another share takes effect` IS A BOOLEAN
    `itself the residue or the whole estate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the will has a residuary disposition` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the will shows a contrary intention` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE Outcome IS ONE OF
    `the gift takes effect`
    `as the will itself provides`
    `a substitutional gift to the beneficiary's surviving children`
    `the share accrues to the other shares`
    `the gift falls into the residue`
    `not disposed of by the will`

GIVEN `the gift` IS A Gift
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 27 saves the gift` IF
        (NOT `the gift`'s `the beneficiary survived the testator`)
    AND `the gift`'s `the beneficiary is a child or other issue of the testator`
    AND `the gift`'s `the interest was not determinable at or before the beneficiary's death`
    AND `the gift`'s `the beneficiary left a child who survived the testator`
    AND (NOT `the gift`'s `given to the beneficiary as a joint tenant`)
    AND (NOT `the gift`'s `the will shows a contrary intention`)

GIVEN `the gift` IS A Gift
GIVETH AN Outcome
`what becomes of the gift` MEANS
    IF `the gift`'s `the beneficiary survived the testator`
    THEN `the gift takes effect`
    ELSE IF `the gift`'s `the will shows a contrary intention`
         THEN `as the will itself provides`
         ELSE IF `section 27 saves the gift` `the gift`
              THEN `a substitutional gift to the beneficiary's surviving children`
              ELSE IF `the gift`'s `a fractional share of the whole or residue, and another share takes effect`
                   THEN `the share accrues to the other shares`
                   ELSE IF (NOT `the gift`'s `itself the residue or the whole estate`) AND `the gift`'s `the will has a residuary disposition`
                        THEN `the gift falls into the residue`
                        ELSE `not disposed of by the will`

§§ `40 -- a will for a person who lacks testamentary capacity`

-- s 40(1): the Court may "make an order authorising -- (a) the making or alteration of a will in specific terms approved by the Court ...
-- on behalf of a person who lacks testamentary capacity". (2): not "unless, at the time when the order is made, the person concerned --
-- (a) is living; and (b) has reached the age of 18 years". s 42(1): the Court "must refuse" unless satisfied of (a) incapacity, (b) the
-- will is one the person could make if not lacking capacity, (c) the applicant is appropriate, (d) adequate steps for representation.
-- s 42(2): it may refuse for any other reason, so this decides only whether the Court MAY make the order.
GIVEN `living` IS A BOOLEAN, `age at the order` IS A NUMBER, `lacks testamentary capacity` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Court is satisfied of section 42(1)(a) to (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Court may authorise a statutory will` IF
        `living`
    AND `age at the order` AT LEAST 18
    AND `lacks testamentary capacity`
    AND `the Court is satisfied of section 42(1)(a) to (d)`
